	)
	(text "Reference. J5 is the external 10 MHz. U13 (74LVC1GU04 + R30) squares it; net REF_BUF.\nX2 is the on-board 10 MHz clipped-sine TCXO, squared by U14 74LVC1G17.\nU15 74LVC1G157: S low = TCXO on I0, S high = REF IN on I1.\nPA6 REF_SEL is pulled down, so a blank chip selects the TCXO.\nPA5 REF_DET is REF_BUF through 1k, for edge counting.\nMux Y goes through 33 ohm and C3 into ADF4351 REFIN.\nX2 pin 1 (OE) is open. This YXC family treats a floating OE as enabled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 327.914 -3.048 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3bd473ae-4e8f-4b0a-9714-53887e17125b")
	)
	(text "ADF4351 3rd-order loop for integer-N transverter LOs (divider 1, VCO 2.2-4.4 GHz, then multiplied). Kv=40 MHz/V. Topology kept: C20 shunt on CP, R14+R20(0R)+C17 shunt, R25 series to Vtune, C31 shunt.\nG(s)=Icp*Kv*Z(s)/(s*N). R22=4.7k so Icp=(code+1)/16*25.5/4.7 mA. Fpfd 10 MHz uses code 0011 = 1.36 mA. Fpfd 2.5 MHz uses code 1111 = 5.43 mA (Icp and N both x4, same gain).\nC20=100p C0G, R14=2.2k, C17=3.3n C0G, R25=2.7k, C31=150p C0G. Third pole 1/(2*pi*R25*C31)=393 kHz.\nSame BW/PM at both PFD settings. At 2.2/2.7/3.1/3.6/4.0/4.4 GHz: 77.7/65.5/58.2/51.6/47.3/43.8 kHz, PM 50.1/50.9/51.0/50.6/50.1/49.4 deg. Third pole is 5.1x BW at 2.2 GHz. At Fpfd 2.5 MHz the sample delay takes about 3-6 deg; PM stays near 45."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 -36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "521174e2-b3ac-46df-8c56-5cb29f4701f4")
	)
	(text "PCB: 1.5 mm hole under each LED with GND via ring (waveguide below cutoff).\nReverse-mount Kingbright KPTL-3216. Light exits the bottom face.\nPWR and COMM are green KPTL-3216CGCK-01 (C598390). \nREF LOCK and SYNTH LOCK are red KPTL-3216SURCK-01 (C598393).\nBlue KPTL-3216QBC-D-01 is on LCSC but Vf is 3.3 V, so it is not used on this 3.3 V rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -97.282 181.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6b95df42-fe13-4c1a-8400-ab8ab2fa5fd0")
	)
	(text "What frequency range on output is required? all the way to 6 GHZ?\nWhat VCC/VDD pins require lowest noise? \nCan regulators be different noise levels on different pins to save $?\nOn Eval Kit for ADF4350, why only two regulators?\nHow does eval kit get away with one set or loop filter Rs and Cs?\nHow should loop filter components be distributed between CP side and TUNE side (to minimize pickup)\nWhat connector layout for board, what enclosure?\nShould MUX and LD outputs be routed to buffers and LEDs directly?\nWhat test points on board?  \n  - 0.025 posts for scope clips?\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 -18.034 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6c39c1b3-5874-4de3-bf60-392c0b2151bb")
	)
	(text "Programming: J8 removed. MCU TX (TXD_M, PB2) drives FT231X RXD.\nFT231X TXD still drives MCU RX (RXD_M, PB3) through R16.\nUPDI is PA0 only, on J12 (UPDI, VDD, GND). Optiboot ersatz reset: DTR - 100 nF - PA4, 10 k to VDD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 464.566 202.692 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c2b32757-1c60-4af0-aad5-c709b1d0e380")
	)
